    "result_text": "Full suite: **60 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\nThe change is implemented and green. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, labelled by its **start** year \u2014 e.g. a 2026-08-15 registration \u2192 `FY26`, matching the hint in `Cp14Tests`).\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (the source for the generated `OwnerDto`)\n- Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` field (`FY<YY>`, derived from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`).\n- Updated `membershipNumber`'s description to state its `-M<YY>` segment now uses the fiscal-year YY.\n- Updated `membershipPoints`' description from \"365 days\" to \"at least one elapsed fiscal year\".\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Added `@Mapping` for `fiscalYear` \u2192 `fiscalYear(owner)`.\n- Changed `membershipNumber` to derive its year segment via `fiscalYearSuffix(...)` instead of the calendar year (`registrationDate.getYear() % 100`).\n- Replaced `tenureDays` (a `ChronoUnit.DAYS`/365-day window) with `tenureFiscalYears`, counting elapsed fiscal years, and awarded tenure points when `>= 1` fiscal year (constant `TENURE_POINTS_FISCAL_YEARS`). A newly created owner still has zero tenure, so it never earns the points (keeps level capped below 4).\n- Added shared helpers `fiscalYear`, `fiscalYearSuffix`, and `fiscalYearStart` so the membership number's year segment and `fiscalYear` always agree; removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\nSince `registrationDate` is already business-day-adjusted before the owner is persisted (in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`), every derived value here reads from the adjusted date automatically.\n\nNote: `2026-08-15` is a Saturday, so the default registration rolls to Monday `2026-08-17` \u2014 still within FY26, confirmed by the audit lines (`...-M26`).",
